== CANON-20 / ADR-0008: `in` is non-associative. `X in A in B` is a parse
== error; the programmer must parenthesize the intended grouping.
Module Diagnostics.InNonAssociative

Main :
    X Integer := 4
    B Bool := X in 1..9 in 1..2
    PutLn(B)
;
